# Failing-first fresh-slot relaunch replays in tests/fm-relaunch-fresh-slot.test.sh, on upstream-lean 6dd37c2a merged in: a herdr ship recorded in an older same-origin clone relaunches into a free slot of this home's clone through the ordinary spawn path (new pane, slot claimed, branch at the old copy's HEAD fetched from the copy because origin lacks it, nothing pushed, record naming the live clone and slot, old pane closed, old copy and its claim left for the old clone's retirement), both through fm-spawn --relaunch and end to end through fm-control relaunch. Origin's branch is used when it already holds the copy's HEAD; an older live branch moves forward; a live branch outside the copy's history, a copy off its branch, and a recorded worktree of another repository refuse; uncommitted work (including an edit an ignored submodule hides) refuses in fm-control before the agent is stopped, and a full live pool defers there; a failure after the slot is claimed and before the new record returns the slot and keeps the old copy; two spellings of one origin match. Each of these 12 fails on 6dd37c2a and passes here. Two guards pass on both: a ship whose home clone has another origin stays where it is, and an old copy another task claims is refused (#176's reassigned-slot refusal) before the fresh path reads from it.
